According to Indonesian regulations, financing, supplies and external staff can only begin to circulate if the disaster zone has been declared a national disaster.
This hasn't happened yet.
“This is still a disaster at the regional level”, said Aulia Arriani, a spokesman for the Indonesian Red Cross.
“After the government says “O’K., this is a national disaster”, we can ask for national aid, but this status has not yet been given.”
The second niet after Friday's earthquake and tsunami in Palu, the friends and families of missing persons were still hopeful that their lovedrever's case would be from those few miracles that ever happen in the event of natural disasters.
