Mexico's AMLO pledges not to use military against civilians
U.S. President-elect Andres Manuel Lopez Obrador has vowed never to use military forces against civilians as the country approaches the 50th anniversary of a bloody reprisal against students.
On Saturday in Tlatelolco Plaza, Lopez Obrador vowed to "never use the military to crush the Mexican people."
