Worldwide Network creator plans to launch a new internet to compete Google and Facebook
Tim Berners-Lee, the creator of the Worldwide Network, is creating a company that aims to rival Facebook, Amazon and Google.
The technology legend’’’’’’’’’’’’’’’’ is a company that’s built by Berners-Lee’’’’’’’’’’s
‘Solid’ allows users to choose where their data is stored and which persons are allowed to have access to certain information.
In an exclusive interview with ‘Fast Company’ Berners-Lee jokingly said that the goal after ‘Inrupt’ is ‘world domination.”
"We've got to do it now," he told this innovative company.
"It's a historic moment."
The app uses Solid technology to allow people to “store their personal data on the network” or a POD”.
It can contain contact lists, lists of things to do, music lists and other personal and professional tools.
It's the same as having available in a browser and at the same time Google Drive, Microsoft Outlook, Slack and Spotify.
What is unique for the storage of personal data on the network is the fact that it remains entirely up to the user what kind of information it will access.
The company calls this "personal empowerment through data."
The idea for Inrupt, according to the company's chief executive, John Bruce, is to bring together the right resources, processes, and skills to help Solid be available to anyone.
The company currently consists of Berners-Leá, Bruce, a security platform purchased by IBM, several developers contracted to work on this project, and a community of volunteer coders.
Starting from this week, tech developers around the world can create their own decentralized apps using the tools available on Inrupt's website.
Berners-Lee said he and his team aren't talking to "Facebook and Google on whether or not to introduce a total change where all their business models are completely overturned at night.
"We don't ask for their permission."
In an ‘Medium’ post published on Saturday, Berners-Leèe wrote that “the mission “is to offer commercial energy and an ecosystem that helps protect the integrity and quality of the new Solid built network."
In 1994, Berners-Lee transformed the internet when he founded the Worldwide Network Consortium at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.
Over the past few months, Berners-Lee has been an influential voite in network impartiality debate.
Even as it establishes Inrupt, Berners-Leé will remain the founder and director of the Worldwide Network consortium, the Network Foundation and the Open Data Institute.
“I’m extremely optimistic about this new era of the network,” Berners-Lee added.
