"When he experiences so many things at such a young age" - he went to the first Olympics at the age of 14 and his father died of cancer three years later - he said it was hard to find someone at the same age who had experienced the same ups and down.
The couple became parents in June of a son named Robert Ray Black-Daley and Daley said his "whole perspective" had changed.
“If you’d asked me last year, all I thought was ‘I’ve got to win a gold medal,’” he said.
“You know what, there are more important things than Olympic gold medals.
