This was the first time that the Navy returned a ship to its builder after delivery.
Little information was given about the reasons for the return, but the media in Germany cited that there were a range of "major defects in software and hardware" that made the spacecraft useless during a war mission.
The problems in the programming were particularly important on Baden-Wuertemberg-class ships because they will be operated by a crew of 120 sailors — as much as half of the ‘Bremen class’’’ ‘old ‘Bremen class’ workforce.”
It was also revealed that the ship was extremely overweight, which reduced its yield and limited the Navy's ability to increase future improvements.
