US-China trade war for Beijing
The first hailings of the U.S.-China trade war were deafening, and as the war is far from an end, a rift between the two countries could pose an advantage for Beijing in the long term, experts say.
U.S. President Donald Trump issued the first warning earlier this year, imposing taxes on major Chinese export goods, including solar panels, steel and aluminum.
The most significant escalation was what happened this week, when the new tariffs affected $200 billion (£150 billion), effectively taxing half of goods that entered the U.S. from China.
Beijing has retaliated every time �“in nature“, most recently imposing tariffs from five to ten percent over $60 billion worth of U.S. goods.
“China has pledged to return the U.S. with the same currency, and the world’s second-largest economic power is unlikely to be delivered soon.
Removing measures from Washington means surrendering their demands, but for China's President Xi Jinping, it would be too embarrassing to be publicly bowed before the US.
However, experts said that if Chine plays its papers properly, the pressures coming from the trade war with the U.S. could positively support China in the long term to reduce the interdependence of these two economies.
“The fact that political decisions, made rapidly both in Washington and in Beijing, could cause economic downturning in each of these countries, is something much more dangerous than what has been seen from abroad” said Abigail Grace, an associate researcher at the new U.S. security research center, which focuses on the Asian continent.
Syria is 'ready' for the return of refugees, foreign minister says
Syria says it is ready for the voluntary return of refugees and is appealing for help to rebuild a war-torn country that has lasted for more than seven years.
Speaking at the United Nations General Assembly, Foreign Minister Walid al-Moualem said conditions in the country are improving.
"Today, the situation in the country is much more stable and secure thanks to the progress made in the fight against terrorism," he said.
The government continues to rehabilitate terrorist-rosted areas to restore normalcy.
Already, there are all the conditions for the voluntary return of refugees to their country, from where they had to leave due to terrorism and unilateral economic measures that hit their daily lives and their well-being.
U.N. estimates that about 5.5 million Syrians have fled the country since the start of the war in 2011.
About sive million others who are still living in the country in need of humanitarian assistance.
Al-Moulem said the Syrian regime would welcome aid to rebuild the devastated state.
But, he stressed that the country would not accept conditional assistance or assistance from countries that sponsored the uprising.
Europe wins "Ryder Cup" trophy in Paris
The European team has won the 2018 Ryder Cup Trophy after beating the U.S. team with a final score of 16.5, at Le Golf National on the exit of Paris, France.
The U.S. has already lost six matches in a row in Europe and has won the trophy in Europe since 1993.
Europe regained its crown after Danish captain Thomas Bjorn's team managed to get the 14.5 points it needed to defeat the United States.
U.S. star Phil Mickelson, who encountered the most difficulties during the tournament, took the first shot into the water and closed his 16th pit with 3 shots more than a certain level, losing the match against Francesco Molinari.
Italian golfer Molinari excelled in all his rounds, becoming 1 of the 4 players who have reached the score 5-0-0, since the current format began to be applied, in 1979.
American Jordan Spieth was beaten 5&4 by the lowest-ranked player in the European team, Danish Thorbjorn Olesen.
The number one player in the world rankings, Dustin Johnson, lost 2 and 1 to Englishman Ian Poulter, who may have played in his latest Ryder Cup final.
Spanish veteran Sergio Garcia, who has played in the eight Ryder Cups, became the most successful European player of all time in this tournament, with 25 career points.
"Usually, I don’t cry but today I can’’’t hold myself.
