We have to “take our hat off”.
They played better than us."
Updations about "Red Tide" (Red Tide): Concentrations in Pinellas, Manatee and Sarasota decrease
Recent reports by the Fish and Live World Commission (FWC) in Florida show an overall drop in red tide concentrations in some areas of Tampa Bay.
According to FWC, there has been an improvement in pollution levels in Pinella, Manatee, Sarasota, Charlotte and Collier - which suggests a decrease in concentrations.
The Red tide has stretched pollution to a length of 130 miles of coastline from north of Pinellas to south of Lee County.
Polluted areas can be found about 10 miles off the coast of the Hillsborough County County Contain, but in fewer areas compared to last week.
Red tide has also been observed in Pasco County.
Over the past week there have been reported average concentrations near or far from shore in the Contain, low and high concentrations in Hillsborough Contentions, data for high concentrations, near or off-shore, in Sarasota County, data for average concentrations in the Charlotte Contents, data for high concentrations, near or away from the coast.
In Content Pinellas, Manatee, Sarasota, Lee, and Collier continue reports of difficulty breathing.
Over the past week, there were no reports of breathing difficulties in northwestern Florida.
